yoyo now builds against yoagent 0.27.1, which carries the #1138 fix: a CA setting that loads no certificates no longer crashes a worker thread. The commit is 552ad28f, titled "Part of #1142", so task 2 is what closes the issue. Build, cargo test (7282 passed, 0 failed), clippy with -D warnings, fmt --check and harness_logic.sh all pass.

The upgrade itself: "0.26" → "0.27" in Cargo.toml, and the lock moved 0.26.8 → 0.27.1. No ReadFileTool/WriteFileTool/BashTool struct literal needed changing.

Claims 0.27 made false, now fixed:
• Image size cap (user-visible change). image_cap.rs said its 20 MiB limit matched yoagent's read_file. Under 0.27 that limit is 3.75 MB and public, so MAX_IMAGE_BYTES now uses yoagent::tools::DEFAULT_MAX_IMAGE_BYTES directly. Before, a 4–20 MB image was attached and then rejected by the provider. Now --image, /add and @path refuse it before reading it. On the real binary, a 4 MB --image exits 1 with (4.0 MB, max 3.75 MB); it was not read. A new test goes through the real read_image_for_add: exactly the cap is read; the cap + 1 byte and 4,000,000 bytes are refused. I updated docs/src/usage/repl.md, the doc line in commands_file.rs, and ARCHITECTURE.md (old claim kept, marked superseded).
• `on_stop` and the output limit. Since 0.27.0, on_stop is called for an answer cut off at the output limit. yoyo installs no on_stop handler, so behaviour is unchanged; I only corrected the comment in output_limit.rs.
• A test outside the task's file list. The full test run caught one failure the task didn't predict. cancel_mid_tool_tests asserted that a history with an unanswered tool call can never produce a second answer. Since 0.27.0, yoagent fills in an error result for that call when the next run starts, so it does. I renamed the test and changed it to check that repair (error flag set, "No result was recorded" text). One consequence: only the check on the restored history can now spot an unanswered call.

Version markers: all 34 yoagent-version-claim markers (ARCHITECTURE.md has 10, two lines carrying two each) were checked against the 0.27.1 source and moved to 0.27. 33 are still true as written, and image_cap.rs was rewritten. The commit body has one line per marker.

Other 0.27 changes that turned out not to matter for yoyo:
• Partial-read guard: yoyo builds its read and write tools without yoagent's read log, so yoyo's own #1094 guard is still the only one.
• Bash colour-code stripping: yoyo runs its own bash tool, so it doesn't apply.
• New sub-agent warning: it goes through tracing, and yoyo installs no tracing output, so nobody sees it.
• `with_max_depth` / `with_max_retry_after`: not wired. The depth cap of 3 is still a convention only.

Left for task 2, posted on #1142: SUPPORTED_IMAGE_FORMATS (src/commands_file.rs:134) still accepts GIF, which 0.27's read_file refuses. I didn't change it: the file is at its size limit, and Anthropic does accept GIF, so whether to drop it depends on the provider.

Live checks: -p "Reply with exactly: ok" printed ok. SSL_CERT_FILE=/dev/null -p hi is still refused cleanly by yoyo's own startup check (exit 1); task 2 decides whether that check stays.
